concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "5 Functions of the CEO"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-5 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The functions of the CEO are: (a) to formulate programs and policies with respect to agricultural research for either or both of the following purposes: (i) identifying agricultural problems of developing countries; (ii) finding solutions to agricultural problems of developing countries; (b) to commission agricultural research by persons or institutions (whether the research is to be conducted in Australia or overseas) in accordance with such programs and policies; and (c) to communicate to persons and institutions the results of such agricultural research; and" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The functions of the CEO are: (a) to formulate programs and policies with respect to agricultural research for either or both of the following purposes: (i) identifying agricultural problems of developing countries; (ii) finding solutions to agricultural problems of developing countries; (b) to commission agricultural research by persons or institutions (whether the research is to be conducted in Australia or overseas) in accordance with such programs and policies; and (c) to communicate to persons and institutions the results of such agricultural research; and"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "216d8d03879e259bbb60bae9f00caca2cc43cc0df04feb9eff3655c6ba6ff9dc" ;
    cof:pageNumber "9"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The CEO must formulate programs and policies for agricultural research." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
