concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-10 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10 Appointment of Commissioners"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-10 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A Commissioner is to be appointed by the Governor-General by written instrument. (2) A Commissioner holds office for the period specified in the instrument of appointment. The period must not exceed 3 years. (3) A person cannot be appointed as a Commissioner if the person is a member of the Council." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A Commissioner is to be appointed by the Governor-General by written instrument. (2) A Commissioner holds office for the period specified in the instrument of appointment. The period must not exceed 3 years. (3) A person cannot be appointed as a Commissioner if the person is a member of the Council."@en ;
