concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-act-1982-sec-24 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "24 Appointment of CEO"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-24 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The CEO is to be appointed by the Governor-General by written instrument. (2) The CEO holds office for the period specified in the instrument of appointment. The period must not exceed 5 years. (3) A person may be appointed as both the CEO and a Commissioner (including the Chair). Performance standard (4) The Minister may, in writing, determine a performance standard for the CEO. Note: Unsatisfactory performance may lead to termination of the CEO’s appointment: see subsection 29C(3). (5) The performance standard is not a legislative instrument." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The CEO is to be appointed by the Governor-General by written instrument. (2) The CEO holds office for the period specified in the instrument of appointment. The period must not exceed 5 years. (3) A person may be appointed as both the CEO and a Commissioner (including the Chair). Performance standard (4) The Minister may, in writing, determine a performance standard for the CEO. Note: Unsatisfactory performance may lead to termination of the CEO’s appointment: see subsection 29C(3). (5) The performance standard is not a legislative instrument."@en ;
